* RESETLED - clears the sync apply watermark (Adabas file 99).
*
* TEST SUPPORT ONLY. sync-verify.cmd runs the same batch numbers on
* every pass, and the applier correctly refuses any batch not newer
* than the ledger - so without this the second test run would skip
* everything and "pass" by doing nothing.
*
* Never run this against a real synchronised pair: the watermark is
* what stops already-applied batches being applied again.
DEFINE DATA LOCAL
1 L VIEW OF LEDGER
  2 STREAM-ID
1 #N (I4)
1 #LINE (A) DYNAMIC
END-DEFINE
*
DEFINE WORK FILE 5 '/sync/work/reset_result.txt' TYPE 'ASCII'
*
RESET #N
FIND L WITH STREAM-ID = 'APPLY'
  ADD 1 TO #N
  DELETE
END-FIND
END TRANSACTION
*
COMPRESS 'LEDGER-RESET removed' #N 'record(s)' INTO #LINE
WRITE WORK FILE 5 VARIABLE #LINE
CLOSE WORK FILE 5
*
END
